{"tag":"P76C","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"1704.04089","version":"1","local":"prop-2","file":"","label":"parallel","number":"2","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{parallel}\nTo a finite bijection\n$f: A \\times C \\to B \\times C$\nwe can associate in a fully equivariant manner a new bijection $\\bar{f}$ with\n\\[\n\\bar{f}((a,c)) = (\\bar{f}_c(a),c)\n\\]\nwhere $\\bar{f}_c:A \\to B$ is a bijection for each $c \\in C$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"theorem","number_from":"counter","labels":["parallel"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"equi.tex","from":253,"to":261},"hash":"sha256:65c816e9c1e1187ab67951af406d96a191c0ad9879ecaa7fa8a0f7ea2c0947c8","minhash":"","census":"1704.04089v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
